src/kdos: the vmdos command shell (boot option shell=kernel)

DOSBox-X's DOS kernel and command shell, run inside the vmdos monitor in
place of FreeDOS. Taken from DOSBox-X (https://github.com/joncampbell123/dosbox-x,
commit 576d8be), GPL-2.0-or-later, with its copyright headers kept; changes
are marked "kdos:". Left out: the GUI, emulated hardware, host folders,
save states, PC-98/DOS/V, and DOSBox-X's Z: utilities.

From DOSBox-X: shell*.cpp, dos*.cpp, drive_fat.cpp, drive_virtual.cpp,
drive_cache.cpp, drives.cpp/.h, dev_con.h, callback.cpp, programs.cpp,
support.cpp, cmdline.cpp (from setup.cpp), bios_disk_kdos.cpp (from
bios_disk.cpp), compat/ (some of its headers; the others are stand-ins).

vmdos's own: glue.cpp (callbacks as V86 #UD traps, coroutines for
DOSBox-X's nested guest runs, configuration, INT 10h), start.cpp (boot,
C:), redir_drive.cpp (VMDOSNET 9P drives, long names), klibc.cpp,
stubs.cpp, compat/dosbox.h, setup.h, control.h, kdos_stubs.h, and
../kdos_host.c (the monitor's side).

rt/: the few pieces of GCC's C++ runtime the shell uses (red-black trees,
lists, type_info and dynamic_cast), from GCC 13.2.0's libstdc++-v3
(GPLv3+ with the GCC Runtime Library Exception). They're built here with
the rest of the shell's flags, so the 486 build gets no P6 instructions
(GCC's prebuilt 32-bit libstdc++.a is for the i686).
